<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="createorgnotification">
  <title>createOrgNotification</title>
  <shortdesc>Create Org Notification.</shortdesc>
  <refbody>
    <section id="createorgnotification-post">
      <title>POST /api/v1/organization/{orgname}/notifications</title>
      <p><b>Authorizations: </b>oauth2_implicit (<b>org:admin</b>)</p>
    </section>
    <section id="createorgnotification-path-parameters">
      <title>Path parameters</title>
      <table>
        <tgroup cols="4">
          <colspec colname="col_1" colwidth="*"/>
          <colspec colname="col_2" colwidth="*"/>
          <colspec colname="col_3" colwidth="*"/>
          <colspec colname="col_4" colwidth="*"/>
          <thead>
            <row>
              <entry>Type</entry>
              <entry>Name</entry>
              <entry>Description</entry>
              <entry>Schema</entry>
            </row>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <entry>
                <p>path</p>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <p>
                  <b>orgname</b>
                </p>
                <p>
                  <i>required</i>
                </p>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <p>The name of the organization</p>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <p>string</p>
              </entry>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
    </section>
    <section id="createorgnotification-request-body-schema">
      <title>Request body schema (application/json)</title>
      <p>Create a notification for an organization namespace</p>
      <table>
        <tgroup cols="3">
          <colspec colname="col_1" colwidth="*"/>
          <colspec colname="col_2" colwidth="*"/>
          <colspec colname="col_3" colwidth="*"/>
          <thead>
            <row>
              <entry>Name</entry>
              <entry>Description</entry>
              <entry>Schema</entry>
            </row>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <entry>
                <p>
                  <b>event</b>
                </p>
                <p>
                  <i>required</i>
                </p>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <p>The event that triggers this notification. Options include <codeph>quota_warning</codeph> and
<codeph>quota_error</codeph>. Warning-type quota limits trigger <codeph>quota_warning</codeph> notifications. Reject-type limits trigger <codeph>quota_error</codeph> notifications. Deleting a quota configuration automatically removes all associated <codeph>quota_warning</codeph> and <codeph>quota_error</codeph> notification rules for that namespace to prevent orphaned settings. Recreating a quota requires setting up new notification rules.</p>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <p>string</p>
              </entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>
                <p>
                  <b>method</b>
                </p>
                <p>
                  <i>required</i>
                </p>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <p>The notification delivery method. Options include <codeph>email</codeph>, <codeph>slack</codeph>, <codeph>webhook</codeph>,
<codeph>quay_notification</codeph>, <codeph>flowdock</codeph>, and <codeph>hipchat</codeph>.</p>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <p>string</p>
              </entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>
                <p>
                  <b>config</b>
                </p>
                <p>
                  <i>required</i>
                </p>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <p>JSON configuration for the notification method. Configuration varies by method
type. For the <codeph>email</codeph> method at the organization level, providing an empty object (<codeph>"config": {}</codeph>) is valid because recipient routing is handled server-side. Notifications are automatically routed to the organization’s <codeph>contact_email</codeph> if configured; otherwise, they are sent to all organization administrators. Unlike repository-level email notifications, no explicit email address is required in <codeph>config</codeph>.</p>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <p>object</p>
              </entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>
                <p>
                  <b>eventConfig</b>
                </p>
                <p>
                  <i>required</i>
                </p>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <p>JSON configuration for filtering which events trigger the notification.</p>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <p>object</p>
              </entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>
                <p>
                  <b>title</b>
                </p>
                <p>
                  <i>optional</i>
                </p>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <p>Optional user-friendly title for the notification.</p>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <p>string</p>
              </entry>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
    </section>
